# Group detail source notice

Selected group creation, name/notes assignment, touch and serialization contracts were studied from KeePass Password Safe2.61.1, copyright2003–2026 Dominik Reichl and contributors, licensed GPL-2.0-or-later. Original selected source snapshots retain their upstream license headers; the preserved source-study license is `source-study/selected/Docs/License.txt.snapshot` in this candidate. The implementation is a bounded source-assisted adapter, with separate local confirmation, input/MAC and XML/content limits.

Original executable and archive carriers remain in their previously recorded local locations. No original executable/archive is copied into this candidate's public-safe preservation inventory or loaded by application execution. The finite comparison helper deliberately loads the separately pinned original managed assembly for synthetic tests only; its call counts and temporal/UUID adapters are recorded separately from application and GUI execution.
